  1348	- <a id="decided-project-spark-2026-11-06"></a>**What Concrete takes from SPARK** (owner, 2026-11-06: "ok do everything", after Claude, Codex, agy and Kimi chose unanimously; the
  1349	  [review](proposals/SPARK.md) items 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 9 and 10).
  1350	  - *Function values with safety preconditions.* A function whose `#[requires]` is a safety
  1351	    precondition is refused as a function value, including through wrappers and specialization. A
  1352	    binding task designs function-type contracts, trait methods included, as a prerequisite for
  1353	    accepting slice 20 (function values), or earlier if a workload pulls it (R-0601); it is never
  1354	    broadened to non-safety contracts.
  1355	  - *Struct invariants.* `#[invariant(...)]` on a struct with private fields holds at every
  1356	    exposure. The definition is written in the spec before the freeze. Revised 2026-11-07 (owner:
  1357	    "ok go ahead all yes then as you said right", approving the recorded recommendation): the source
  1358	    feature moves from the structs slice (slice 9) to the modules slice (slice 17), where field
  1359	    privacy exists.
  1360	  - *Facts at a point.* `assert(e) by thm(...)` extends [OD79](#od79). Its role is strictly
  1361	    separate from `#[proof]`: `#[proof]` discharges the function's obligations, `assert(e) by
  1362	    thm(...)` establishes one fact at one point, and the theorem's hypotheses are fully discharged.
  1363	  - *Observable events.* Core gets an extensible observable-event kind now, which also protects
  1364	    secret wipes (R-0602); device semantics come later.
  1365	  - *Unused permissions.* A permission that justifies nothing is a fact that a `Concrete.toml`
  1366	    policy may refuse; the decided refusals (an unmatched `#[proof]`, a duplicate
  1367	    `#[may_not_terminate]`) stay.
  1368	  - *Measures.* Lexicographic measures come when a workload needs them (R-0605).
  1369	  - *Assurance.* Assurance is a set of separate named, versioned properties per module, each with
  1370	    its scope, evidence and coverage, not a ladder (R-0606).
  1371	- <a id="decided-project-runtime-2026-11-06"></a>**Trap line, default layout and spec version** (owner, 2026-11-06: "ok do everything", after Claude, Codex, agy and Kimi chose unanimously).
  1372	  - *The trap line* ([OD101](#od101)'s form, spec obligation O4): `concrete: trap: <kind> at
  1373	    <path>:<line>:<col> (site <id>)`, the path relative to the project root with forward slashes,
  1374	    line and column 1-based. Extended 2026-11-08 by the [foundation decision](#foundation-q10): a
  1375	    column counts bytes, and a tab counts one byte.
  1376	  - *Default struct layout:* declaration order, natural alignment defined exactly per target, the
  1377	    size rounded up to the alignment, and zero-sized fields taking no bytes. It is not a C ABI
  1378	    promise (R-0502).
  1379	  - *Spec version:* every output carries one `spec_version`, in one header covering every record
  1380	    (JSON lines included): 0.x before the freeze, 1.0 at A2c, bumped by every normative change and
  1381	    checked in CI. It is distinct from the product's 1.0 (R-0603).
  1382	- <a id="decided-project-lean-root"></a>**A minimal root** (owner, 2026-11-06: "keep the folders and
  1383	  root of the new compiler simple and lean"). The root and the new compiler's folders stay small:
  1384	  the top-level entries and the immediate entries under `docs/` and `scripts/` are those listed in
  1385	  [scripts/checks/root_inventory.txt](../scripts/checks/root_inventory.txt), which a root check
  1386	  enforces, and something comes back from `legacy/` only in the change that needs it. This keeps the
  1387	  [restart](#decided-project-restart)'s minimal day-one root (R-0558) after the move.
  1388	- <a id="decided-project-outside-readers"></a>**The outside readers** (owner, 2026-11-06: "me but also
  1389	  agy and codex and kimi if it's available"). The outside-reader pass (R-0559) is done by the owner and
  1390	  independent models: agy (Gemini), Codex, and Kimi when available. They read the browsable owner view of the
  1391	  integrated spec. The pass runs before the freeze (A2c) and again for each feature
  1392	  ([long-term changes](#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06)). <a id="outside-readers-ordering"></a>*Reading
  1393	  order* (owner, 2026-11-07: "ok go ahead all yes then as you said right", approving the recorded
  1394	  recommendation): Codex, agy and Kimi read first; every point one of them finds unclear is recorded
  1395	  and resolved before the owner's formal read and before the freeze. A real design question still
  1396	  goes to the owner. Kimi's absence, when it is unavailable, is recorded rather than waited on.
  1397	- <a id="decided-project-contracts"></a>**Contracts and termination in verified growth** (row P18,
  1398	  2026-11-05). No source `old`, quantifier, implication or snapshot construct (OD117); entry, exit and
  1399	  frame properties are stated as Lean theorems (a source frame clause would be a new owner decision);
  1400	  spec functions have a body and are total (OD115); an ordinary function can get its own termination
  1401	  proof, with no total-function category (OD116).
  1402	- <a id="decided-project-refusals"></a>**The refusal list** (rows P16, P17a, P17b, 2026-11-05). The
  1403	  statuses in `PHILOSOPHY.md` stand; default arguments are a permanent refusal; compile-time
  1404	  evaluation and broad `#[cfg]` reopen only with a workload, a proof story, phase separation, an audit
  1405	  report and a new owner decision.
  1406	- <a id="decided-project-review"></a>**Review** (owner, 2026-10-18, reaffirmed 2026-11-04: "always codex
  1407	  should check everything"). Codex reviews every change, plan, specification, decision row and piece
  1408	  of infrastructure before it is published or brought to the owner. A second, independent reviewer
  1409	  (Kimi, Grok or agy/Gemini) reviews as well when one is available, as the owner required for cleanup
  1410	  branches on 2026-10-28; when none is (quota, credit or sign-in), its absence is recorded with the
  1411	  review and never assumed. A review never replaces the gates. Extended 2026-11-08 (owner: "also
  1412	  remember we have agy not only codex kimi and claude"): every branch gets an agy review beside the
  1413	  Codex and Kimi reviews. agy cannot read files, so its prompt carries the diff and the context it
  1414	  needs and ends with a required verdict line. (The coordinator's relay added that agy can also act
  1415	  as a writer.)
  1416	- <a id="decided-project-throughput"></a>**Development throughput** (2026-10-22). The development
  1417	  feedback loop (landing, review, CI) is a priority track beside the main sequence
  1418	  ([record](archive/roadmap-2026-11/ROADMAP_DECISIONS.md#2026-10-22--development-throughput-priority)).
  1419	- <a id="decided-project-supersession"></a>**Editorial supersession of legacy task directions**
  1420	  (2026-11-03). The new-compiler and restructure decisions supersede in-place repairs and migration of
  1421	  frozen compiler internals; the archived task bodies keep their history and regression obligations
  1422	  ([record](archive/roadmap-2026-11/ROADMAP_DECISIONS.md#2026-11-03--editorial-supersession-of-legacy-task-directions)).
