     `docs/proposals/SLICE1_BRIEF.md:108-110` treats `checked_exits` as an existing contract, while `:124-128` requires changes only to syntax, semantics, checker, and `checked_no_implicit_traps`. But `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Slice1.lean:720-737` proves that **every accepted program exits**, which directly contradicts the accepted, trapping program at `docs/proposals/SLICE1_BRIEF.md:74-76`. `checked_exits`, its supporting trap-freedom proof at `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Slice1.lean:687-718`, and their documentation must also be revised.

